{#
  NAV ITEM LABEL — the word stack behind the roll-on-hover.

  THIS IS THE CODE COUNTERPART OF FIGMA'S Nav_item (410:66301). That component
  is instanced in two places in the comp — three times in the header (446:37196)
  and twice in the footer (568:39273, the Email Me and Set a Meeting actions) —
  and for a long time the code answered that with two independent implementations
  that happened to agree. The rules-above-and-below mechanic is still written out
  twice, once per host, because the two genuinely differ in their resting state;
  but the roll is identical in both and lives here, once.

  WHAT THE HOSTS STILL OWN. This macro emits the label and nothing else — no
  colour, no borders, no opacity, no padding. .site-header__link and
  .site-footer__action keep every one of those. The footer's items used to sit at
  a 70% resting dim and lift to full on hover; 568:39273 states their colour
  outright instead, so --footer-dim was removed and the resting state is now just
  the colour the host sets. Swapping a bare {{ label }} for {{ navItem(label) }}
  is meant to be invisible until someone hovers.

  THE COPY COUNT IS LOAD-BEARING, and this is the only place it is written down.
  The roll lifts the stack by exactly one line, so N turns need N+1 copies —
  something has to be sitting in the slot when the motion stops. One turn, two
  copies. If the roll ever goes back to three turns, this is the file that grows
  two more spans, and _nav-item.css is the file that changes the travel; nothing
  else in the codebase knows the number.

  Copy 2 is aria-hidden, so the accessible name is the label once rather than
  twice, and it is user-select:none in CSS so dragging across a nav does not put
  "ContactContact" on the clipboard. With no hover (touch) or under reduced
  motion the stack never moves and the spare is simply clipped out of sight.

  USAGE
    {% raw %}{% from "components/nav-item.njk" import navItem %}
    <a class="site-header__link" href="/#contact">{{ navItem("Contact") }}</a>{% endraw %}
#}

{%- macro navItem(label) -%}
<span class="nav-item__roll"
  ><span class="nav-item__stack"
    ><span class="nav-item__word">{{ label }}</span
    ><span class="nav-item__word" aria-hidden="true">{{ label }}</span
  ></span
></span>
{%- endmacro -%}
